- Right segment: \((0, 2)\) to \((2, 4)\) (increasing, slope \(1\), \(y \in [2, 4]\)).  

The \(y\)-ranges of the segments do not overlap, and each segment is strictly increasing (no repeated \(y\)-values). Thus, it passes the horizontal line test and is one-to-one.


