The graph is a straight line with slope \(-1\) (from \((-3, 5)\) to \((5, -3)\)). A strictly decreasing line is always one-to-one, as no two \(x\)-values produce the same \(y\)-value. Thus, it passes the horizontal line test and is one-to-one.


