The graph is the upper semicircle \(x^2 + y^2 = 16\) (centered at the origin, radius 4). Horizontal lines intersect this semicircle at two points (e.g., \(y = 2\) intersects at \((\pm 2\sqrt{3}, 2)\)). Thus, it fails the horizontal line test and is not one-to-one.


