Assume symmetry (i.e., \(a = b = t\)) to simplify calculations. This is justified by the AM-GM inequality, which suggests the minimum sum \(a + b\) for fixed \(ab\) occurs when \(a = b\). Substituting \(a = b = t\) into the constraint:  
